## 0. Orient (every session)

1. Read `docs/{{SLUG}}/` in order: PROGRESS → PLAN → ARCHITECTURE → DECISIONS → DESIGN (before any
   visual, motion or sound work) → RESEARCH.
<!-- if:monetization -->
   Then MONETIZATION before any money, data, consent or analytics work.
<!-- /if:monetization -->
<!-- if:release -->
   Then RELEASE and `store/` before building a release or changing any store text.
<!-- /if:release -->
2. Run the baseline in `CLAUDE.md`. If it is red, fixing it is the task. Trust the run, not
   PROGRESS's claim. First decide whether the code or the environment is red.
3. Take the exact next step from PROGRESS "In progress". If there is none, take the first unmet
   acceptance criterion in PLAN.

**When the docs conflict:**
- PROGRESS and PLAN decide *what next*; DECISIONS and ARCHITECTURE decide *how*;
- RESEARCH decides *the facts*; DESIGN decides *the look and feel*;
<!-- if:monetization -->
- MONETIZATION decides *money and data*;
<!-- /if:monetization -->
<!-- if:release -->
- RELEASE and `store/` decide *how a release is built and proved, and what the store pages say*;
<!-- /if:release -->
- this skill restates invariants; DECISIONS is their source, so if they differ, fix this file.

