**Feel is tuned on a device.** Motion and sound numbers in DESIGN are *Proposed* starting values.
Change them only after watching or listening on a simulator or phone. Record old → new, and why, in
DESIGN.

**Ship small vertical slices** through the pipeline: plan written → skeptics → freeze contracts →
build (≥ 3 looks on anything visible) → integrate (cold launch) → analyze + full suite →
adversarial review → fixer → mutation proofs → confirming look and every gate → docs → one commit.

**Never fabricate an API.** Read the installed source of every package and SDK you call
([TODO: where the package cache and SDK live on this machine]). Read the platform implementation,
not only the shared interface. When the source and a research brief disagree, the source wins. Pin
surprising library behaviour in small tests under `docs/{{SLUG}}/reference/<lib>/`, with a README
saying they are demos, not code to copy.

**Every guard is seen to fail.** A new test counts only after you have removed its fix or feature
and watched it fail, in an isolated copy (never the shared tree), by assertion (a compile error
proves nothing).

